# build / local artifacts
*.log
*.tar
*.tar.gz
build/
bld/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Session artefacts, never committed (vibeic-eda 2026-07-30, same class as
# vibe-ic#720). Sixteen of these were sitting untracked-and-unignored for eight
# to eleven days — `.bak` copies of Dockerfile and the fork ledgers, build logs
# from a failed 0.2.27 attempt, an ALIGN verification dump, and a ledger backup
# directory. Untracked-but-not-ignored is the state one `git add -A` turns into
# a commit, which is precisely why this repo forbids `-A`; a rule nobody has to
# remember beats a rule everybody must.
#
# `*.log` was already here and did NOT cover `build_0.2.27.log.attempt1` —
# `.log` is not at the end. That is the shape of the whole problem: a rule
# written for the case its author met.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
*.log.*
*.out
_ledger_backups/
*.merged.json
